  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1145 PM CDT Fri Aug 7 2026\n\nSurface analysis shows a cold front pushing through the southernmost \ncounties of the CWA this evening with the only clouds betraying\nthe front's exact location. Otherwise, skies are generally \ncloud free but visible satellite imagery was tinted with \nwildfire smoke at 7kft to 12kft. Thankfully, it's expected to \nstay elevated through at least Sunday. \n\nThe upper pattern reveals our cold front is tied to a shortwave trof \nworking through Ontario and a ridge spinning over the Desert \nSouthwest. Our pattern should become more zonal over the next few \ndays as the trofing continues east and the ridging southwest of\nhere dampens.",
